  "title": "Ex 9.2 · Is 2n² − 4n + 31 always prime?",
  "prompt": "Statement: for every natural number $n$, the integer $2n^2 - 4n + 31$ is prime. This statement is false. Disprove it with a counterexample.",
  "answer_format": "Integer values for every variable, like a = 4, b = 2, c = 2.",
