        "2n^2 - 4n + 31"
      ]
    }
  },
  "answer": "n = 31",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Trying n = 1, 2, 3, … gives primes for a while.",
    "Pick n so that every term of 2n² − 4n + 31 shares a factor with 31."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Take $n = 31$: $2 \\cdot 31^2 - 4 \\cdot 31 + 31 = 31(62 - 4 + 1) = 31 \\cdot 59 = 1829$, which is not prime.",
    "So the statement is false."
  ],
